% M18-coverage-T11 / D-0234: a global_cardinality RULE C shortfall under a decision now
% LEARNS, and its line carries the CROSSED bound.
%
% Deciding k <= 2 pushes x1, x2 <= 2 (int_le) and c3 >= 2 (c3 + k >= 4) before the
% global_cardinality they wake runs, so only x3 can still take 3 and rule C pushes
% hi(c3) := 1 below lo(c3) = 2. That push used to fail factless. Now it is the conflict, with
% the push's facts (x1 <= 2, x2 <= 2: the bounds that exclude 3) and the count's LIVE lower
% bound c3 >= 2, which the push's own reason does not carry and without which the line is
% not implied. x3 holds 3, its indicator is cleared by literal axioms, and it is named with
% no literal.
%
% SAT (k = 3), so every rup on the page is really checked (D-0053).
var 1..4: k :: output_var;
var 1..3: x1 :: output_var;
var 1..3: x2 :: output_var;
var 1..3: x3 :: output_var;
var 0..3: c3 :: output_var;
constraint int_le(x1,k);
constraint int_le(x2,k);
constraint int_lin_le([-1,-1],[c3,k],-4);
constraint fzn_global_cardinality([x1,x2,x3],[3],[c3]);
solve :: int_search([k,x1,x2,x3,c3], input_order, indomain_min, complete) satisfy;
